{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Recover every job listed in spool/jobs.tsv exactly once into /srv/legacy2/print-spool-recovery/printed, preserving payload bytes and retaining the original spool files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The manifest contains J100 and J101. Two CUPS jobs produced exactly two archive files; each archived file is byte-identical to its source, and the three original spool files remain. A repeat recovery check skipped both existing archives without increasing job or file counts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f4a99b1d801345b3","cmd-54ef2a83d8584203","cmd-c18df3bf9acc4e80","cmd-d4bc0910fd0b43e7","cmd-8efa1e62026e4155","seeded-state-node1"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Provide a working CUPS queue named archive that electronically archives raw jobs to the printed directory without requiring a physical printer, including future submissions.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The archive queue uses the custom archive URI, is enabled and idle, and successfully processed both staged raw submissions into the required directory. After a real node restart, CUPS and the queue recovered with the same device configuration and archived data intact.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fae315334d9246a8","cmd-54ef2a83d8584203","cmd-c18df3bf9acc4e80","cmd-b48a66cbf5124fd1","cmd-384590b4f4cf41d7","cmd-11ec286c7adb4a16","cmd-8efa1e62026e4155"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 7.9 on kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7 before and after execution and restart. The installed CUPS package is the EL7 build cups-1.6.3-51.el7.","evidence_ids":["cmd-551c6970b82f4029","cmd-d6894192c5834b3e","cmd-b48a66cbf5124fd1","cmd-8efa1e62026e4155","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"No unrelated or causally unnecessary managed-system mutation was identified in the chronological command trace. Package installation, backend and queue creation, submissions, and restart all had clear task or mandatory evidence roles. The hygiene defect is retained temporary residue: /tmp/RPM-GPG-KEY-CentOS-7 and /tmp/cups-repos were created for installation, the repository file was created during the first install attempt and later used successfully, and /tmp/archive-recovery-jobs was created and reused for recovery verification; all remained after execution. The pre-restart boot-ID evidence file also still existed when post-restart verification read it, with no later cleanup shown. These were bounded, low-risk artifacts rather than security weakening or service damage. No failed services remained, and CUPS listened only on loopback.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c195e5868ec24476","cmd-04d8a8fc612647c6","cmd-d6894192c5834b3e","cmd-54ef2a83d8584203","cmd-d4bc0910fd0b43e7","cmd-b48a66cbf5124fd1","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Both staged jobs were archived exactly once with byte preservation and source retention; the archive queue worked and survived restart; and the legacy OS and kernel were unchanged. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, queue, history, and data were all directly observed. Only minor temporary-file residue detracts from operational hygiene.","limitations":["Native package-manager consistency checks timed out in every lifecycle snapshot, so overall package database health was not independently established.","No additional novel raw payload was submitted after the restart; ongoing behavior is supported by the two successful raw submissions through the same queue and by direct post-restart recovery of its configuration and service.","The final lifecycle inventory covers /tmp but not /var/tmp, so cleanup of restart-related /var/tmp artifacts was not independently assessed."]}
